[{"explanation":{"text":["Let CP was 100 for A originally","A sells article to B at 10% profit,","CP for B = 100 + 10% of 100 = 110","Now, B sells it A again with loss 10%","Now, CP for A this time = 110 - 10% of 110 = 99","A makes Profit = 110 - 99 = 11","%profit for A = $\\frac{11×100}{100}$ = 11%","","Second Method","It could be easily shown by net percentage change graphic.","100(A) == 10%(Profit) ⇒110(B) == 10%(Loss) ⇒ 99(A)","","In this transaction A makes a profit of (110 - 99 = 11%) 11%","","[10% on selling to B and 1% profit on buying back from B]"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0ab29578f984a2b1b897e","text":["A sells an article to B at a profit of 10% B sells the article back to A at a loss of 10%. In this transaction:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":" A neither losses nor gains","image":"","_id":"65e0ab29578f984a2b1b897f"},{"text":"A makes a profit of 11%","image":"","_id":"65e0ab29578f984a2b1b8980"},{"text":" A makes a profit of 20%","image":"","_id":"65e0ab29578f984a2b1b8981"},{"text":" B loses 20%","image":"","_id":"65e0ab29578f984a2b1b8982"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:04:57.274Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:04:57.274Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the Cost price of the Chair is X.","SP = X - 25% of X","720 = 0.75X","X = 960","CP = Rs. 960","So, To gain 25%, SP would be","= 960 + 25% of 960 =Rs. 1200","","Short-cut","CP of chair = $\\frac{100}{75}$"," × 720 = Rs. 960","To gain 25%, SP = $\\frac{125}{100}$"," × 960 = Rs. 1200"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0ab9b578f984a2b1b8a08","text":["If a man were to sell his chair for Rs. 720, he would lose 25%. To gain 25% he should sell it for:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 1,200","image":"","_id":"65e0ab9b578f984a2b1b8a09"},{"text":"Rs. 1,000  ","image":"","_id":"65e0ab9b578f984a2b1b8a0a"},{"text":"Rs. 960","image":"","_id":"65e0ab9b578f984a2b1b8a0b"},{"text":"Rs. 900","image":"","_id":"65e0ab9b578f984a2b1b8a0c"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:06:51.065Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:06:51.065Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["n the case where loss and gain percentage is common on same selling price, always a loss incurs in total deal. And this can be calculated by a short-cut:","Loss on total deal,","=$(\\frac{Common loss or gain percentage}{10})^2=(\\frac{20}{10})^2$=4%","","","Alternatively, It can be also calculated through Graphic Change Method: This can be given by,","100 == 20% gain ⇒ 120 == 20% loss ⇒ 96","Loss = 4% (As 100 became 96)"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0ac48578f984a2b1b8aa2","text":["A man sold two chairs at Rs. 1200 each. On one he gained 20% and on the other he loss 20%. His gain or loss in the whole transaction is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"1% loss     ","image":"","_id":"65e0ac48578f984a2b1b8aa3"},{"text":"2% loss     ","image":"","_id":"65e0ac48578f984a2b1b8aa4"},{"text":"4% loss     ","image":"","_id":"65e0ac48578f984a2b1b8aa5"},{"text":"5% loss     ","image":"","_id":"65e0ac48578f984a2b1b8aa6"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:09:44.825Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:09:44.825Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the cost price be Rs. 100","then the mark up price which is 30% above the cost price,","Mark price = (100 + 30% of 100) = Rs. 130","Shopkeeper gives a discount of 10% on mark up price, then the","Selling Price = (130 - 10% of 130) = Rs. 117","Gain = 117 - 100 = Rs. 17","%gain=$\\frac{17×100}{100}$=17%","","","Short Cut method:","100(CP) == 30%↑ ⇒ 130(MP) == 10%↓ ⇒ 117(SP)","Gain = 17%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0aca6578f984a2b1b8b30","text":["A shopkeeper marks his goods 30% above his cost price but allows a discount of 10% at the time of sale. His gain is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"21%  ","image":"","_id":"65e0aca6578f984a2b1b8b31"},{"text":"20%  ","image":"","_id":"65e0aca6578f984a2b1b8b32"},{"text":"18%  ","image":"","_id":"65e0aca6578f984a2b1b8b33"},{"text":"17%  ","image":"","_id":"65e0aca6578f984a2b1b8b34"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:11:18.535Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:11:18.535Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let his CP = Rs. 100.","Marked Price = 100 + 25% of 100 = 125.","Now, discount = $\\frac{25}{2}$% on MP","So, SP = 125 - $\\frac{25}{2}$% of 125 = Rs. 109.375.","%Gain = 9.375%.","","Alternatively use graphic change method:","100(CP) == 25% Up ⇒ 125(MP) == 12.5%down ⇒ 109.375","%Profit = 9.375%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0ad5f578f984a2b1b8bc6","text":["A tradesman marks his goods at 25% above the cost price and allows purchasers a discount of $\\frac{25}{2}$%, his profit is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"8%  ","image":"","_id":"65e0ad5f578f984a2b1b8bc7"},{"text":"8.5%  ","image":"","_id":"65e0ad5f578f984a2b1b8bc8"},{"text":"8.625%  ","image":"","_id":"65e0ad5f578f984a2b1b8bc9"},{"text":"9.735%  ","image":"","_id":"65e0ad5f578f984a2b1b8bca"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:14:23.309Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T16:58:50.113Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the CP be Rs. 100, then SP = 100 + 14.28% of 100 = Rs. 114.28","(As Profit = 14.28%)","This profit is arrived after giving discount of 11.11% on the marked price.","Let the marked price be x","X - 11.11% of X = 114.28","X × $\\frac{100−11.11}{100}$","  = 114.28","X = $\\frac{114.28×100}{8889}$","   = Rs. 128.56, which is more than 28.56% of CP."],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0af87578f984a2b1b8d20","text":["After allowing a discount of 11.11%, a trader still makes a gain of 14.28%. At how many percent above the cost price does he mark on his goods?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":" 28.56%","image":"","_id":"65e0af87578f984a2b1b8d21"},{"text":"35%","image":"","_id":"65e0af87578f984a2b1b8d22"},{"text":"22.22%","image":"","_id":"65e0af87578f984a2b1b8d23"},{"text":"None of these","image":"","_id":"65e0af87578f984a2b1b8d24"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:23:35.119Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:23:35.119Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the price of shirt and trouser be Rs. 100 and Rs. 200 respectively.","Then, price of set of shirt and trouser = Rs. 300.","After giving 30% discount on the set,","Selling Price = 300 - 30% of 300 = 210.","Total Discount on Set = 90.","And Discount on shirt is 20% alone,","SP of shirt alone = 100 - 40% of 100 = 60.","Rs. 40 is the discount on shirt then Rs. 50 must be the discount on the trouser.","So, discount on trouser = $\\frac{50×100}{200}$","  = 25%."],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0ae1c578f984a2b1b8c6e","text":["The marked price of a shirt and trousers are in the ratio 1:2. The shopkeeper gives 40% discount on the shirt. If the total discount in the set of the shirt and trousers is 30%, the discount offered on the trousers is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"15%","image":"","_id":"65e0ae1c578f984a2b1b8c6f"},{"text":"20%","image":"","_id":"65e0ae1c578f984a2b1b8c70"},{"text":"25%","image":"","_id":"65e0ae1c578f984a2b1b8c71"},{"text":"30%","image":"","_id":"65e0ae1c578f984a2b1b8c72"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:17:32.612Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:17:32.612Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the dealer buys 3 kg, 4 kg and 5 kg.","Price of total dry fruits = 3 × 100 + 4 × 80 + 5 × 60 = Rs. 920","SP = 920 + 50% of 920 = 1380","Hence,","Price of mix dry fruits per kg = $\\frac{1380}{12}$"," = Rs. 115"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0afdb578f984a2b1b8db4","text":["A dealer buys dry fruits at Rs. 100, Rs. 80, and Rs. 60 per kilogram. He mixes them in the ratio 3:4:5 by weight and sells at a profit of 50%. At what price per kilogram does he sell the dry fruits?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 80","image":"","_id":"65e0afdb578f984a2b1b8db5"},{"text":"Rs. 100","image":"","_id":"65e0afdb578f984a2b1b8db6"},{"text":"Rs 95","image":"","_id":"65e0afdb578f984a2b1b8db7"},{"text":"None of these","image":"","_id":"65e0afdb578f984a2b1b8db8"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:24:59.831Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:24:59.831Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the marked price = Rs. 100","Then the cost price = 80% of 100 = Rs. 80","After allowing 12% discount on MP,","SP become = Rs. 88.","% profit = $\\frac{8×100}{80}$","  = 10%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0b01f578f984a2b1b8dbf","text":["The cost price of an article is 80% of its marked price for sale. How much per cent does the tradesman gain after allowing a discount of 12%?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"20%","image":"","_id":"65e0b01f578f984a2b1b8dc0"},{"text":"12%","image":"","_id":"65e0b01f578f984a2b1b8dc1"},{"text":"10%","image":"","_id":"65e0b01f578f984a2b1b8dc2"},{"text":"8%","image":"","_id":"65e0b01f578f984a2b1b8dc3"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:26:07.869Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:26:07.869Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Discount on one shirt,","= 25% of 320 = $\\frac{320×25}{100}$","  = Rs. 80","Hence, number of shirt he must buy to get a rebate of Rs. 400 = $\\frac{400}{80}$"," = 5"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0b110578f984a2b1b8e40","text":["A merchant has announced 25% rebate on prices of ready-made garments at the time of sale. If a purchaser needs to have a rebate of Rs. 400, then how many shirts, each costing Rs. 320, should he purchase?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"10","image":"","_id":"65e0b110578f984a2b1b8e41"},{"text":"7","image":"","_id":"65e0b110578f984a2b1b8e42"},{"text":"6","image":"","_id":"65e0b110578f984a2b1b8e43"},{"text":"5","image":"","_id":"65e0b110578f984a2b1b8e44"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:30:08.507Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:30:08.507Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Marked Price = 25000.","After first discount it become,","= 25000 - 20% of 25000 = 20000.","After second discount, it becomes","= 20000 - 5% of 20000 = 19000.","So, SP = 19000.","CP for the man who bought it, as he spends 1000 on repair.","= 19000 + 1000 = 20000","Profit = 25000 - 20000 = 5000.","%Profit = $\\frac{5000×100}{20000}$","  = 25%","","Short-Cut","25000(MP) == 20%(Disc.) ⇒ 20000 == 5%(disc.) ⇒19000(CP)","Spends on repair = Rs. 1000","Then, CP becomes = 19000 + 1000 = 20000","Profit = 5000","% profit = $\\frac{5000×100}{20000}$","  = 25%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0ae7c578f984a2b1b8c74","text":["A dealer buys an article marked at Rs. 25,000 with 20% and 5% off. He spends Rs. 1,000 for its repairs and sells it for Rs. 25,000. What is his gain or loss per cent?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"loss of 25%","image":"","_id":"65e0ae7c578f984a2b1b8c75"},{"text":"gain of 25%","image":"","_id":"65e0ae7c578f984a2b1b8c76"},{"text":"gain 10%","image":"","_id":"65e0ae7c578f984a2b1b8c77"},{"text":"loss of 10%","image":"","_id":"65e0ae7c578f984a2b1b8c78"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:19:08.663Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:19:08.663Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let CP = 100","Then, MP = 100 + 20% of 100 = 120","Now, SP = 120 - 10% of 120 = 108","Gain = 108 - 100 = 8","%Gain = $\\frac{8×100}{100}$","  = 8%","","Short-cut","100(CP) == 20%(up) ⇒ 120(MP) == 10%(disc.) ⇒ 108","% gain = 8%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0af15578f984a2b1b8d14","text":["The marked price of a radio is 20% more than its cost price. If a discount of 10% is given on the marked price, the gain per cent is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"15","image":"","_id":"65e0af15578f984a2b1b8d15"},{"text":"12","image":"","_id":"65e0af15578f984a2b1b8d16"},{"text":"10","image":"","_id":"65e0af15578f984a2b1b8d17"},{"text":"8","image":"","_id":"65e0af15578f984a2b1b8d18"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:21:41.744Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:21:41.744Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["In such cases, always loss occurs. It can be calculated by this formula,","=$(\\frac{loss or gain percentage}{100})^2$=4","","That is 4% of loss","","Graphic Change method","100 == 20%(loss) ⇒ 120 == 20%(gain) ⇒ 96","% Loss = 4%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0b181578f984a2b1b8efc","text":["I sold two watches for Rs. 300 each, one at loss of 20% and other at the profit of 20%. What is the percentage of loss (-) or profit (+) that resulted from the transaction?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"(+)4","image":"","_id":"65e0b181578f984a2b1b8efd"},{"text":"(-)1","image":"","_id":"65e0b181578f984a2b1b8efe"},{"text":"(+)1  ","image":"","_id":"65e0b181578f984a2b1b8eff"},{"text":"(-)4","image":"","_id":"65e0b181578f984a2b1b8f00"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:32:01.034Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:32:01.034Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["CP = Rs. 95.","Then SP = 95 + 10% of 95 = Rs. 104.5","Let MP = X. He gives 5% commission on MP.","So,","SP = X - 5% of X","SP = 0.95X","104.5 = 0.95X","X = $\\frac{104.5}{0.95}$=100","","Thus, MP = Rs. 110","","Short-cut","95 == 10%(gain) ⇒ 104.5 == 5%(Commission) ⇒ 109.72 (= 110)"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0b1e2578f984a2b1b8f02","text":["A shopkeeper wishes to give 5% commission on the marked price of an article but also wants to earn a profit of 10%. If his cost price is Rs. 95, then marked price is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 100","image":"","_id":"65e0b1e2578f984a2b1b8f03"},{"text":"Rs. 110","image":"","_id":"65e0b1e2578f984a2b1b8f04"},{"text":"Rs. 120","image":"","_id":"65e0b1e2578f984a2b1b8f05"},{"text":"Rs. 130","image":"","_id":"65e0b1e2578f984a2b1b8f06"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:33:38.537Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:33:38.537Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["=(A + B) - $\\frac{AB}{100}$","","= (10 + 5) - $\\frac{10×5}{100}$","","= 14.5%","Let MP = X","Now,","X - 14.5% of X = 171(Selling Price)","0.855X = 171","X = 200","Hence, MP = Rs. 200","","Going through options,","200(MP) == 10%(disc.) ⇒ 180 == 5%(disc.) ⇒ 171(CP)"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0bce4578f984a2b1b9b72","text":["The selling price of an article after giving two successive discounts of 10% and 5% on the marked price is Rs. 171. What is the marked price?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 200","image":"","_id":"65e0bce4578f984a2b1b9b73"},{"text":"Rs. 220","image":"","_id":"65e0bce4578f984a2b1b9b74"},{"text":"Rs. 240","image":"","_id":"65e0bce4578f984a2b1b9b75"},{"text":"Rs. 250","image":"","_id":"65e0bce4578f984a2b1b9b76"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T17:20:36.650Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T17:20:36.650Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["CP of bicycle = 100×$\\frac{2850}{114}$","  = Rs. 2500","SP for the profit of 8% = 108×$\\frac{2500}{100}$","   = Rs. 2700"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0bd58578f984a2b1b9b78","text":["By selling a bicycle for Rs. 2,850, a shopkeeper gains 14%. If the profit is reduced to 8%, then the selling price will be:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 2600     ","image":"","_id":"65e0bd58578f984a2b1b9b79"},{"text":"Rs.2700","image":"","_id":"65e0bd58578f984a2b1b9b7a"},{"text":"Rs. 2800","image":"","_id":"65e0bd58578f984a2b1b9b7b"},{"text":"Rs. 3000","image":"","_id":"65e0bd58578f984a2b1b9b7c"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T17:22:32.553Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T17:22:32.553Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Use Formula,","Equivalent Discount = (A + B) - $\\frac{AB}{100}$"," where A = First Discount, B =Second Discount.","Equivalent Discount = (20 + 10) - $\\frac{20×10}{100}$","","Equivalent Discount = 30 - 2 = 28%","","Graphic Change Method","100 == 20%(disc.) ⇒ 80 == 10%(disc.) ⇒ 72","Equivalent discount = 28%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0bbcf578f984a2b1b97b1","text":["Two successive discount of 10% and 20% are equivalent to a single discount of:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"30%","image":"","_id":"65e0bbcf578f984a2b1b97b2"},{"text":"28%","image":"","_id":"65e0bbcf578f984a2b1b97b3"},{"text":"26%","image":"","_id":"65e0bbcf578f984a2b1b97b4"},{"text":"25%","image":"","_id":"65e0bbcf578f984a2b1b97b5"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T17:15:59.602Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T17:15:59.602Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Assume the cost price = 100 and selling price = 120","Then, when price of petrol is reduced","Cost price become 60 and selling price = 160","Profit increased = 100%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0bda2578f984a2b1b9bc8","text":["A driver of auto rickshaw makes a profit of 20% on every trip when he carries 3 passengers and the price of petrol is Rs. 30 a litre. Find the % profit for the same journey if he goes for 4 passengers per trip and the price of petrol reduces to Rs. 24 litres? (revenue per passenger is same)"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"20%","image":"","_id":"65e0bda2578f984a2b1b9bc9"},{"text":"33.33%","image":"","_id":"65e0bda2578f984a2b1b9bca"},{"text":"100%","image":"","_id":"65e0bda2578f984a2b1b9bcb"},{"text":"65.66%  ","image":"","_id":"65e0bda2578f984a2b1b9bcc"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T17:23:46.604Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T17:23:46.604Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Marked Price = 2000","SP after first Discount of 20% = 2000 - 20% of 2000 = 1600","SP after second Discount of 10% = 1600 - 10% of 1600 = 1440","Now, the final selling price at cash = 1440 - 5% of 1440 = Rs. 1368","","Shortcut by using Graphic Change","2000(MP) == 20%(disc.) ⇒ 1600 == 10%(disc.) ⇒ 1440 == 5%(disc.) ⇒ 1368(SP)"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0ad95578f984a2b1b8c4f","text":["A bicycle marked at Rs. 2,000, is sold with two successive discount of 20% and 10%.An additional discount of 5% is offered for cash payment. The selling price of the bicycle at cash payment is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 1,368","image":"","_id":"65e0ad95578f984a2b1b8c50"},{"text":"Rs. 1,468","image":"","_id":"65e0ad95578f984a2b1b8c51"},{"text":"Rs. 1,568","image":"","_id":"65e0ad95578f984a2b1b8c52"},{"text":"Rs. 1,668","image":"","_id":"65e0ad95578f984a2b1b8c53"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T16:15:17.293Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T16:15:17.293Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["He sells only 900 grams when he takes the money for 1 kg.","and","he sells at a 8% profit (20% markup, 10% discount)","Hence, his selling price is Rs. 108 for 900 grams","% profit = $\\frac{18}{90}$×100","   = 20%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0bdd9578f984a2b1b9c1d","text":["A dishonest dealer marks up the price of his goods by 20% and gives a discount of 10% to the customer. He also uses a 900 gram weight instead of a 1 kilogram weight. Find his percentage profit due to these maneuvers?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"8%","image":"","_id":"65e0bdd9578f984a2b1b9c1e"},{"text":"12%","image":"","_id":"65e0bdd9578f984a2b1b9c1f"},{"text":"20%","image":"","_id":"65e0bdd9578f984a2b1b9c20"},{"text":"16%  ","image":"","_id":"65e0bdd9578f984a2b1b9c21"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T17:24:41.083Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T17:24:41.083Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Total cost = type + Printing + paper, ink","= 1000 + 120 × 9 + 540 = 2620","Net sum to be recovered = Rs. 2882","Total magazine sold 784 for = 784 × 2.75 = 2156","Sum obtained from advertisement = 2882 - 2156 = Rs. 726"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0be96578f984a2b1b9d30","text":["The cost of setting up the type of a magazine is Rs. 1000. The cost of running the printing machine is Rs. 120 per 100 copies. The cost of paper, ink and so on is 60 paise per copy. The magazines are sold at Rs. 2.75 each. 900 copies are printed, but only 784 copies are sold. What is the sum to be obtained from advertisements to give profit of 10% on the cost?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 730","image":"","_id":"65e0be96578f984a2b1b9d31"},{"text":"Rs. 720","image":"","_id":"65e0be96578f984a2b1b9d32"},{"text":"Rs. 726","image":"","_id":"65e0be96578f984a2b1b9d33"},{"text":"Rs. 736","image":"","_id":"65e0be96578f984a2b1b9d34"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T17:27:50.077Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T17:27:50.077Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let MP = X","CP = 1440","SP = 1440 + 25% of 1440 = Rs. 1800","SP = MP - 25% of MP","SP = X - 25% of 100","SP = X - 0.25X","1800 = 0.75X","X = 2400","MP = Rs. 2400","","Short-Cut","Let the marked price = Rs. x","Hence,","$75×\\frac{x}{100}=1440×\\frac{125}{100}$","","⇒ $\\frac{1440×125}{75}$","  = Rs. 2400"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0bc66578f984a2b1b9ae8","text":["A dealer allows his customer a discount of 25% and still gains 25%. If cost price of a radio is Rs. 1440, its marked price is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":" Rs. 2500","image":"","_id":"65e0bc66578f984a2b1b9ae9"},{"text":" Rs. 2440 ","image":"","_id":"65e0bc66578f984a2b1b9aea"},{"text":"Rs. 2400","image":"","_id":"65e0bc66578f984a2b1b9aeb"},{"text":"Rs. 2020","image":"","_id":"65e0bc66578f984a2b1b9aec"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T17:18:30.355Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T17:18:30.355Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["100 --- 10%↓(1st discount) → 90 --- 5%↓ → 85.5","Net discount = 100 - 85.5 = 14.5%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e14066457911e9895d6f3e","text":["Ajay bought a motor cycle for Rs. 50,000. 2 years later he sold it to Vijay at 10% less of the cost price. Vijay spend 5% of the purchasing price on its maintenance. Later Vijay displayed the sale price of his motorcycle Rs. 50,000. Chetan wanted to purchase it at 15% discount but Vijay gave him two successive discounts of 10% and 5% instead of 15% in one time. What is the actual discount availed by Chetan?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"15%","image":"","_id":"65e14066457911e9895d6f3f"},{"text":"15.5%","image":"","_id":"65e14066457911e9895d6f40"},{"text":"14.5%","image":"","_id":"65e14066457911e9895d6f41"},{"text":"16.5%","image":"","_id":"65e14066457911e9895d6f42"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T02:41:42.121Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T02:41:42.121Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["He buys 1100 gram instead of 1000 gram.","Suppose he bought 1100 grams for Rs. 1000.","","While selling,","He sells only 900 grams when he takes the money for 1 kg.","Now, according to the problem,","he sells at a 8% profit (20% markup, 10% discount).","Hence, his selling price is Rs. 1080 for 900 grams.","Now,","1100 grams for Rs. 1000","Hence, 1188 grams for Rs. 1080","Selling: 900 grams for Rs. 1080","Hence, % profit =$\\frac{288}{900}$×100 = 32%","(using goods left by goods sold formula)."],"images":[]},"_id":"65e14015457911e9895d6ed5","text":["A dishonest dealer marks up the price of his goods by 20% and gives a discount of 10% to the customer. Besides, he also cheats both his supplier and his buyer by 100 grams while buying or selling 1 kilogram. Find the percentage profit earned by the shopkeeper?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"20%","image":"","_id":"65e14015457911e9895d6ed6"},{"text":"25%","image":"","_id":"65e14015457911e9895d6ed7"},{"text":"32%","image":"","_id":"65e14015457911e9895d6ed8"},{"text":"33%","image":"","_id":"65e14015457911e9895d6ed9"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T02:40:21.570Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T02:40:21.570Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["100 (Initial CP) --- 20%↑ (initial profit) → 120(SP)","120 (SP) --- 25%↑ → 150 (New SP)","Let x be the new Cost price","Selling Price = 150","x × 1.25 = 150","x = 120","% change = $\\frac{120−100}{100}$×100","     = 20%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e14103457911e9895d6fa1","text":["A retailer increase the selling price by 25% due to which his profit percentage increase from 20% to 25%. What is the percentage increase in cost price ?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"20%","image":"","_id":"65e14103457911e9895d6fa2"},{"text":"30%","image":"","_id":"65e14103457911e9895d6fa3"},{"text":"25%","image":"","_id":"65e14103457911e9895d6fa4"},{"text":"50%","image":"","_id":"65e14103457911e9895d6fa5"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T02:44:19.129Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T02:44:19.129Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["120 (CP) --- 15% ↓(loss) → 102 (SP)","Mental work:","10% of Rs. 120 = 12","5% of Rs 120 = 6"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e1413c457911e9895d6fa7","text":["A watch costing Rs. 120 was sold at a loss of 15%. At what price was it sold?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 112","image":"","_id":"65e1413c457911e9895d6fa8"},{"text":"Rs. 135","image":"","_id":"65e1413c457911e9895d6fa9"},{"text":"Rs.102","image":"","_id":"65e1413c457911e9895d6faa"},{"text":" Rs. 110","image":"","_id":"65e1413c457911e9895d6fab"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T02:45:16.648Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T02:45:16.648Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Set up cost = Rs. 2800","Paper etc = Rs. 1600","Printing cost = Rs. 3200","Total cost = Rs. 7600","Total sale price = 1500 × 5 = 7500","Let amount obtained from advertising be x then,","(7500 + x) - 7600 = 25% of 7500","x = 1975"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e14177457911e9895d6fb3","text":["The cost of setting up a magazine is Rs. 2800. The cost of paper and ink etc is Rs. 80 per 100 copies and printing cost is Rs. 160 per 100 copies. In last month 2000 copies were printed but only 1500 copies could be sold at Rs. 5 each. Total 25% profit on the sale price was realized. There is one more resource of income from magazine which is advertising. What sum of money obtained from the advertising in magazine?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 1750","image":"","_id":"65e14177457911e9895d6fb4"},{"text":" Rs. 2350","image":"","_id":"65e14177457911e9895d6fb5"},{"text":"Rs. 1150","image":"","_id":"65e14177457911e9895d6fb6"},{"text":"Rs. 1975","image":"","_id":"65e14177457911e9895d6fb7"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T02:46:15.686Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T02:46:15.686Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Suppose he buy 1 quintal of Rice in Rs.150.","10% is spoiled so he now have to sell of 90 kg remaining).","But he has to make a profit of 20%,so he will sell","90kg for Rs. 180","This means his selling price is Rs. 200 per quintal."],"images":[]},"_id":"65e141b3457911e9895d6fb9","text":["A person bought a certain quantity of rice at the rate of Rs. 150/quintal. 10% of the rice was spoiled. At what rate(per quintal) should he sell the remaining rice to earn 20% profit."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 180  ","image":"","_id":"65e141b3457911e9895d6fba"},{"text":" Rs. 200","image":"","_id":"65e141b3457911e9895d6fbb"},{"text":"Rs. 210","image":"","_id":"65e141b3457911e9895d6fbc"},{"text":"Rs. 220","image":"","_id":"65e141b3457911e9895d6fbd"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T02:47:15.435Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T02:47:15.435Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the marked price be 100","100 == 20% ↓(discount) ⇒ 80 == 10%↓ (discount) ⇒ 72(CP) == 10%↑ (interior) ⇒ 79.2(Total CP)","Now, selling price would be 25% above the Total cost price.","SP = 79.2 + 25% of 79.2","SP = 99","Now, On comparing,","100 ⇒ 800000","99 ⇒ $\\frac{800000}{100}$×99","    ⇒ 7,92,000","So,","SP = Rs. 7,92,000"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e14205457911e9895d6fcb","text":["Kamal bought a house, whose sale price was Rs. 8 lakh. He availed 20% discount as an early bird offer and then 10% discount due to cash payment. After that he spent 10% of the cost price in interior decoration and lawn of the house. At what price should he sell the house to earn a profit of 25%?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 9 lakh","image":"","_id":"65e14205457911e9895d6fcc"},{"text":" Rs. 7.99 lakh","image":"","_id":"65e14205457911e9895d6fcd"},{"text":"Rs. 7.92 lakh","image":"","_id":"65e14205457911e9895d6fce"},{"text":" Rs. 7 lakh","image":"","_id":"65e14205457911e9895d6fcf"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T02:48:37.962Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T02:48:37.962Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let CP's be Rs. 1000 each, their respective SP will be,","1000 == 25%↑ ⇒ 1250 [person calculating profit on the CP]","1000 == 33.33%↑ ⇒ 1333.33 [The person calculating his profit on SP: 25% of SP = 33.33% of CP]","The difference turned out to be = 83.33. This has occured when we have assumed the CP as 1000. But, we are given difference of Rs. 100","So, on comparing,","83.33 = 1000","1 = $\\frac{1000}{83.33}$","","100 = $\\frac{1000}{83.33}$×100","   = Rs. 1200"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e142b7457911e9895d7114","text":["Find the selling price of goods if two salesmen claim to make 25% profit each, one calculating it on cost price while another on the selling price, the difference in the profits earned being Rs. 100 and selling price being the same in both the cases?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 1200 .  ","image":"","_id":"65e142b7457911e9895d7115"},{"text":"Rs. 1600","image":"","_id":"65e142b7457911e9895d7116"},{"text":"Rs. 2400","image":"","_id":"65e142b7457911e9895d7117"},{"text":"Rs. 2500","image":"","_id":"65e142b7457911e9895d7118"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T02:51:35.432Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T02:51:35.432Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Cost price of 25 kg = Rs. (15 x 14.50 + 10 x 13) = Rs. 347.50.","Sell price of 25 kg = Rs. (25 x 15) = Rs. 375.","profit = Rs. (375 — 347.50) = Rs. 27.50.","",""],"images":[]},"_id":"65e146e1457911e9895d729d","text":["Ajay bought 15 kg of dal at the rate of Rs 14.50 per kg and 10 kg at the rate of Rs 13 per kg. He mixed the two and sold the mixture at the rate of Rs 15 per kg. What was his total gain in this transaction ?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs 1.10","image":"","_id":"65e146e1457911e9895d729e"},{"text":" Rs 11","image":"","_id":"65e146e1457911e9895d729f"},{"text":"Rs 16.50","image":"","_id":"65e146e1457911e9895d72a0"},{"text":"Rs 27.50","image":"","_id":"65e146e1457911e9895d72a1"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T03:09:21.733Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T03:09:21.733Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["CP = 100, SP (with tax) =120",""," ","","New   SP = 100 - 5 = 95",""," ",""," Effective discount = 120 - 95 = 25 ",""," ","","So, at SP of 95 ----> discount = 25",""," ","","and      at SP of 3325 -----> discount = $\\frac{25}{95} \\times 3325 = 875$"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e14677457911e9895d7291","text":["Rahul went to purchase a Nokia mobile handset, the shopkeeper told him to pay 20% tax if he asked the bill. Rahul manages to get the discount of 5% on the actual saleprice of the mobile and he paid the shopkeeper Rs. 3325 without tax. Besides he manages to avoid to pay 20% tax on the already  discounted price, what is the amount of discount that he has gotten?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"750","image":"","_id":"65e14677457911e9895d7292"},{"text":"375","image":"","_id":"65e14677457911e9895d7293"},{"text":"875","image":"","_id":"65e14677457911e9895d7294"},{"text":"525","image":"","_id":"65e14677457911e9895d7295"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T03:07:35.144Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T03:07:35.144Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["33.33% profit means there is one part water and 3 part is pure wine. so the required ratio of water and wine in the mixture is 1:3","",""],"images":[]},"_id":"65e146af457911e9895d7297","text":["In what ratio should water and wine be mixed so that after selling the mixture at the cost price a profit of 33.33% is made?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"1:4","image":"","_id":"65e146af457911e9895d7298"},{"text":"1:3","image":"","_id":"65e146af457911e9895d7299"},{"text":"2:3","image":"","_id":"65e146af457911e9895d729a"},{"text":"3:4","image":"","_id":"65e146af457911e9895d729b"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T03:08:31.048Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T03:08:31.048Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the amount of remaining apple be x and cost price be Rs y/kg","","20% loss, SP = y × (100 – 20)/100 = 0.8y","","30% profit, SP = 1.3y","","20% profit, SP = 1.2y","","Total profit = Sum of profits by selling bad and good apples","","⇒ (x + 20) × 1.2y = (x × 1.3y + 20 × 0.8y)/y","","⇒ 1.2x + 24 = 1.3x + 16","","⇒ 8 = 0.1x","","∴ x = 80 kg","","Total amount of apples = x + 20 = 100 kg","","⇒ Cost of 1 kg of apple = Rs 6800/100 = Rs 68/kg"],"images":[]},"_id":"672a2516deff9f3130db0643","text":["A shopkeeper buys some quantity of apples for Rs 6800. Out of all the apples, 20 kg were found bad condition and he had to sell them at 20% loss. To get a total profit of 20% the remaining apples have to be sold at 30% profit. What is the cost price of apples per kg? (in Rs)"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"34","image":"","_id":"672a2516deff9f3130db0644"},{"text":"68","image":"","_id":"672a2516deff9f3130db0645"},{"text":"17","image":"","_id":"672a2516deff9f3130db0646"},{"text":"100","image":"","_id":"672a2516deff9f3130db0647"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T14:00:54.979Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T14:00:54.979Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let CP for A be 20x","","And CP for B be 10x","","Since A earns a profit of 10%","","Therefore CP of A = 22x","","SP for B = 8x","","Therefore their combined SP = 30x","","Combined CP = 30x","","since CP = SP ","","Hence there is no profit no loss.",""],"images":[]},"_id":"672a2c4fdeff9f3130db07ae","text":["A and B buy two horses, price for A's horse is twice the price for B's horse. A sells it for a profit of 10% B sells it at a loss of 20% loss find their overall profit or loss percentage"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"10% profit","image":"","_id":"672a2c4fdeff9f3130db07af"},{"text":"10% loss","image":"","_id":"672a2c4fdeff9f3130db07b0"},{"text":"no profit no loss","image":"","_id":"672a2c4fdeff9f3130db07b1"},{"text":"5% profit","image":"","_id":"672a2c4fdeff9f3130db07b2"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T14:31:43.380Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T14:31:43.380Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Profit = SP - CP","","Profit% = $\\frac{(profit × 100)}{CP}$","","Let the cost price of 100 kg = Rs 100","","But while buying he makes a profit of 20%","","He buys 120 kg in Rs. 100","","So his cost price of 100 kg = $\\frac{(100 × 100)}{120}$ = $\\frac{500}{6}$.","","He makes a profit of 20% while selling","","He sells 100 kg in Rs. 120","","So, his selling price of 100 kg = Rs. 120","","His actual profit = 120 - $\\frac{500}{6}$ = $\\frac{220}{6}$","","His profit% = {$\\frac{(220/6)}{(500/6)}$} × 100 = 44%"],"images":[]},"_id":"672a2e16deff9f3130db0853","text":["A dishonest shopkeeper misleads while using weigh machine, makes a profit of 20% while buying as well as while selling his goods. Find his actual gain% in the whole process.",""],"images":[],"options":[{"text":" 36%","image":"","_id":"672a2e16deff9f3130db0854"},{"text":"44%","image":"","_id":"672a2e16deff9f3130db0855"},{"text":"38%","image":"","_id":"672a2e16deff9f3130db0856"},{"text":"50%","image":"","_id":"672a2e16deff9f3130db0857"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T14:39:18.390Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T14:39:18.390Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Suppose Ravi bought the mobile at Rs. x","","Ravi sold the mobile to Rohan at 11% profit","","So,","","CP for Rohan = 1.11x","","⇒ x × $\\frac{111}{100}$ = 1.11x","","Rohan sold the phone to Sohan at 12% profit","","So,","","CP for Sohan = 1.11 × 1.12 × x","","⇒ 1.11x × $\\frac{112}{100}$","","⇒ 1.11 × 1.12 × x","","Sohan paid Rs. 12432 for the mobile","","So,","","⇒ 1.11 × 1.12 × x = 12432","","⇒ x = 10000","","Hence, Ravi bought the mobile at Rs. 10000"],"images":[]},"_id":"672a2f81deff9f3130db08fc","text":["Ravi sold a mobile to Rohan at 11% profit and Rohan sold the same mobile to Sohan at 12% profit. If Sohan paid Rs 12432 for the mobile, then at what price did Ravi buy the mobile?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 12000","image":"","_id":"672a2f81deff9f3130db08fd"},{"text":"Rs. 11000","image":"","_id":"672a2f81deff9f3130db08fe"},{"text":"Rs. 10000","image":"","_id":"672a2f81deff9f3130db08ff"},{"text":"Rs. 9000","image":"","_id":"672a2f81deff9f3130db0900"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T14:45:21.591Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T14:45:21.591Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Total marked price = 200 × Rs 30 + 160 × Rs 25 = Rs 10000","","S.P. of Rs 30 marked notebooks = 30 × $\\frac{(100 – 30)}{100}$ = Rs 21","","S.P. of Rs 25 notebooks = 25 × $\\frac{(100 – 20)}{100}$ = Rs 20","","Total sales = 200 × 21 + 160 × 20 = Rs 7400","","Overall discount = $\\frac{(M.P. – S.P.)}{M.P}$ × 100","","⇒ $\\frac{(10000 – 7400)}{10000}$ × 100 = 26%",""],"images":[]},"_id":"672a30f5deff9f3130db0903","text":["Two types of notebooks marked at Rs 30 and Rs 25 are sold in the market. If the discount% offered on Rs 30 notebook and Rs 25 notebook are 30% and 20%, what is the overall discount%? [The total numbers of Rs 30 notebooks and Rs 25 notebooks sold are 200 and 160 respectively.]"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"25","image":"","_id":"672a30f5deff9f3130db0904"},{"text":"26","image":"","_id":"672a30f5deff9f3130db0905"},{"text":"27","image":"","_id":"672a30f5deff9f3130db0906"},{"text":"28","image":"","_id":"672a30f5deff9f3130db0907"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T14:51:33.046Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T14:51:33.046Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let, the CP of the motor car be Rs 100","","SP = 100 - (8% of 100)","","⇒ 100 - ($\\frac{100}{100}$) × 8 = (100 - 8) = Rs. 92","","Now, he gives a 20% discount on MRP","","80% of MRP = Rs 92","","MRP = ($\\frac{92}{80}$) × 100 = Rs 115","","If he had offered a discount of only 12%","","Then, SP = 115 - (12% of 115)","","⇒ 115 - ($\\frac{115}{100}$) × 12 ","","⇒ (115 - 13.8) = Rs. 101.2","","Hence, profit = (101.2 -100) = Rs 1.2","","Therefore, profit % = ($\\frac{1.2}{100}$) × 100 = 1.2%"],"images":[]},"_id":"672a322edeff9f3130db09a2","text":["During a sale, a trader reduced the selling price of a motor car by offering a 20% discount. In this process, he incurred a loss of 8%. What would have been his profit percent, if he had instead offered a 12% discount?",""],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"1.2%","image":"","_id":"672a322edeff9f3130db09a3"},{"text":"3.4%","image":"","_id":"672a322edeff9f3130db09a4"},{"text":"3%","image":"","_id":"672a322edeff9f3130db09a5"},{"text":"2.5%","image":"","_id":"672a322edeff9f3130db09a6"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T14:56:46.551Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T14:56:46.551Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the cost price of the article be 100x","","⇒ Selling price = 112x (using multiplying factor)","","If he had purchased it for 12% less and sold it for Rs 9 less,","","Cost price = 100x × 0.88","","⇒ 88x","","⇒ Selling price - Cost price = Profit","","⇒ 112x - 9 - 88x = 88x × $\\frac{27}{100}$","","⇒ 24x - 9 = $\\frac{2376x}{100}$","","⇒ x(24 - 23.76) = 9","","⇒ x = $\\frac{9}{0.24}$","","⇒ x = 37.5","","⇒ Original cost price = 100x = 3750"],"images":[]},"_id":"672a3c97deff9f3130db0de8","text":["A person sells an article at a profit of 12% If he had purchased it for 12% less and sold it for Rs. 9 less, he would have gained 27%. What is the original cost price of the article?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 3750","image":"","_id":"672a3c97deff9f3130db0de9"},{"text":"Rs. 4500","image":"","_id":"672a3c97deff9f3130db0dea"},{"text":"Rs. 4250","image":"","_id":"672a3c97deff9f3130db0deb"},{"text":"Rs. 4000","image":"","_id":"672a3c97deff9f3130db0dec"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"profit_and_loss","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T15:41:11.356Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T15:41:11.356Z","__v":0}]